A||||3||rodmcneill||Disconnecting steering rack.||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||12-12-2001||12:06 AM||||I am in the process of pulling my steering rack(installing inner-outer tie rods)I managed to get everthing off, loosened, even the 4 bolts holding the rack in place. Do you drop the rack then disconnect the steer shaft universal. It has this plastic shield around it do you just peel it back? Are you supposed to mark it when you take it off. Its getting late and I am getting tired.||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT GT 87||12-12-2001||12:52 AM||||It is easier to un do the steering from the passenger compartment.Take the bolt out completely, if stuck on shaft , wedge open with a screwdriver till free then remove  and pull everything down and out.......||||reg||1
Z||000002||AnimalGT||12-12-2001||01:00 AM||||From where you're at with it, I would do the following things to make it easier:  <BR>-pull the plastic shield back behind the u-joint and put a long screwdriver through the u-joint to hold it back <BR>-completely remove the steer shaft to rack pinch bolt (11mm IIRC)<BR>-use a chisel to spread the u-joint apart, this will let the rack fall if the mounting bolts are out, so be careful<BR>-don't worry about marking the rack's position to the u-joint, it's machined so that it can only go back together the proper way<BR>All this aplies to a '84-'87 only, I haven't worked on an '88 yet.<BR>Have fun,<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000003||rodmcneill||12-12-2001||02:00 AM||||Thanks for the replies, finally got it out. That was a really dirty job, I guess there is something to be said for keeping your front end degreased. At least going back in it will be cleaner with new parts. I will have to give Rodney Dickman a call tomorrow and order a rack bushing, I might as well do it all when its apart.||||reg||10
